## 🚨 BUG 1: Firebase Not Working on iOS — White Screen

### Problem
App shows white screen on iOS because `Firebase.initializeApp()` crashes — no `GoogleService-Info.plist` for iOS.

### Fix
In `lib/main.dart`, wrap ALL Firebase calls in try/catch:

```dart
@pragma('vm:entry-point')
Future<void> _firebaseMessagingBackgroundHandler(RemoteMessage message) async {
  try { await Firebase.initializeApp(); } catch (_) {}
}

void main() async {
  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
  
  // Firebase — may fail on iOS if plist missing
  try {
    await Firebase.initializeApp();
    FirebaseMessaging.onBackgroundMessage(_firebaseMessagingBackgroundHandler);
  } catch (e) {
    debugPrint('Firebase init skipped: $e');
  }
  
  // ... rest of init
}
```

**IMPORTANT:** Search the ENTIRE codebase for `Firebase.initializeApp()` and `FirebaseMessaging` calls. Wrap ALL of them in try/catch. There may be calls in:
- `lib/main.dart`
- Auth providers
- Notification services
- Any realtime/lifecycle files

