## 🚨 BUG 2: Token Expiry — Data Disappears After Hours

### Problem
After a few hours, API calls return 401 (token expired). The app shows empty data instead of refreshing the token or redirecting to login.

### Fix
In `lib/core/api/api_service.dart`, add a Dio interceptor for 401 handling:

```dart
_dio.interceptors.add(InterceptorsWrapper(
  onError: (DioException error, handler) async {
    if (error.response?.statusCode == 401) {
      // Try refresh token
      final refreshToken = await TokenStore.getRefreshToken();
      if (refreshToken != null) {
        try {
          final res = await Dio().post(
            '${AppConstants.baseUrl}/auth/refresh-token',
            data: {'refreshToken': refreshToken},
          );
          final newToken = res.data['accessToken'];
          final newRefresh = res.data['refreshToken'];
          
          // Save new tokens
          await TokenStore.saveTokens(newToken, newRefresh);
          
          // Retry original request with new token
          error.requestOptions.headers['Authorization'] = 'Bearer $newToken';
          final retryResponse = await _dio.fetch(error.requestOptions);
          return handler.resolve(retryResponse);
        } catch (_) {
          // Refresh failed — clear tokens and go to login
          await TokenStore.clearAll();
          // Navigate to login (use a global navigator key)
        }
      }
    }
    handler.next(error);
  },
));
```

**Also ensure:**
- `TokenStore` has methods: `getRefreshToken()`, `saveTokens(access, refresh)`, `clearAll()`
- On login, BOTH `accessToken` AND `refreshToken` are saved
- Token keys: Customer=`hajiz_token`+`hajiz_refresh`, Business=`hajiz_business_token`+`hajiz_business_refresh`, Craftsman=`hajiz_craftsman_token`+`hajiz_craftsman_refresh`

