## 🚨 BUG 5: Android Push Notifications Not Showing

### Problem
FCM notifications don't show when app is closed on Android.

### Fix
1. Ensure `flutter_local_notifications` is configured:

```dart
// In main.dart or a notification service:
final FlutterLocalNotificationsPlugin flutterLocalNotificationsPlugin =
    FlutterLocalNotificationsPlugin();

Future<void> initNotifications() async {
  const android = AndroidInitializationSettings('@mipmap/ic_launcher');
  const ios = DarwinInitializationSettings();
  await flutterLocalNotificationsPlugin.initialize(
    const InitializationSettings(android: android, iOS: ios),
  );
  
  // Create notification channel for Android
  const channel = AndroidNotificationChannel(
    'hajiz_channel', 'حاجز',
    description: 'إشعارات حاجز',
    importance: Importance.high,
  );
  await flutterLocalNotificationsPlugin
      .resolvePlatformSpecificImplementation<AndroidFlutterLocalNotificationsPlugin>()
      ?.createNotificationChannel(channel);
}
```

2. Handle foreground messages:
```dart
FirebaseMessaging.onMessage.listen((RemoteMessage message) {
  final notification = message.notification;
  if (notification != null) {
    flutterLocalNotificationsPlugin.show(
      notification.hashCode,
      notification.title,
      notification.body,
      const NotificationDetails(
        android: AndroidNotificationDetails('hajiz_channel', 'حاجز',
          importance: Importance.high, priority: Priority.high),
        iOS: DarwinNotificationDetails(),
      ),
    );
  }
});
```

3. In `AndroidManifest.xml`, ensure:
```xml
<meta-data android:name="com.google.firebase.messaging.default_notification_channel_id"
    android:value="hajiz_channel"/>
```

